 ## Overview
-Simplex Noise is a gradient-based procedural noise function that generates continuous scalar fields by interpolating contributions from the corners of a simplex grid (tetrahedra in 3D) [S3, unofficial][S4]. It solves the directional artifacts inherent in cubic-grid noise (like classic Perlin noise) by using a skewed triangular/tetrahedral lattice [S4][S6, unofficial]. It scales to higher dimensions with $O(n^2)$ complexity, compared to $O(n 2^n)$ for classic noise, and requires fewer multiplications [S6, unofficial].
