 ## Background
-Simplex Noise was introduced as an improvement over Perlin noise to reduce computational complexity and directional artifacts [S6, unofficial]. It uses a simplex grid (tetrahedra in 3D) instead of a cubic grid [S3, unofficial]. It is widely used in procedural generation for terrain, textures, and volumetric data [S2, S6, unofficial].
+Simplex Noise was introduced as an improvement over Perlin noise to reduce computational complexity and improve scaling to higher dimensions [S6, S7, unofficial]. It uses a simplex grid (tetrahedra in 3D) instead of a cubic grid [S3, S4, unofficial]. It is used for generating volumetric data and isosurfaces [S2, S3, unofficial].
 
